KG42.register("rules-2ca6bf86402e102b45285abe",{"id":"09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R005","paper":"09-local_flexibility","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R005","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"The local market-clearing outcome determines the final activation fee payable by the DSO to the aggregators. Scope: Activation fees for acquired conditional DSO flexibility services in the EcoGrid 2.0 local flexibility market. Condition: The acquired flexibility service is conditional. Payments are split into a reserve part and an activation part. Scope: Payment structure for conditional DSO flexibility services in EcoGrid 2.0. Condition: The service is conditional. The DSO pays only the reserve price. Scope: Payment for an acquired conditional DSO flexibility service that is not activated. Condition: The conditional service is not activated. The DSO must pay an activation fee to the aggregators. Scope: Activation payment for an acquired conditional DSO flexibility service. Condition: The conditional service is activated.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.local","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E001","source":"clearing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g03-e12"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Activation fees for acquired conditional DSO flexibility services in the EcoGrid 2.0 local flexibility market. | Activation payment for an acquired conditional DSO flexibility service. | Payment for an acquired conditional DSO flexibility service that is not activated. | Payment structure for conditional DSO flexibility services in EcoGrid 2.0.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g03-e12"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local market-clearing outcome determines the final activation fee payable by the DSO to the aggregators. Scope: Activation fees for acquired conditional DSO flexibility services in the EcoGrid 2.0 local flexibility market. Condition: The acquired flexibility service is conditional.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g03-e12"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Payments are split into a reserve part and an activation part. Scope: Payment structure for conditional DSO flexibility services in EcoGrid 2.0. Condition: The service is conditional.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The DSO pays only the reserve price. Scope: Payment for an acquired conditional DSO flexibility service that is not activated. Condition: The conditional service is not activated.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The DSO must pay an activation fee to the aggregators. Scope: Activation payment for an acquired conditional DSO flexibility service. Condition: The conditional service is activated.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g02-e26"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E02","location":{"location_id":"src-65c3762894-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3 EcoGrid 2.0 services","anchor_text":"Fig. 2. Sketch of a capacity limitation service. occasion. To be able to rely on such ﬂexibility ser","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Payments for conditional services are split into a reserve part and an activation part. If a conditional service is not activated, the DSO only pays the reserve price."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e26","location":{"location_id":"src-65c3762894-p08-c2r3__v141-a-M01-activation","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.4 Activation benefit evaluation for conditional services","anchor_text":"In the case of conditional services, the DSO has to pay an activationng fee to the aggregators. The ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the case of conditional services, the DSO has to pay an activation fee to the aggregators. The DSO has to make the decision whether it is beneficial to activate the service or not. Activation costs are specified by the aggregators as part of their bids, hence the final activation cost is determined by the outcome of the market clearing. The service activation signal can be sent up to one hour before the service delivery period. At this point, the uncertainty of load forecasts is smaller, as the delivery period is closer.\nTo estimate the benefit of service activation, load samples are generated in the same manner as before. However, at this point lead time is much smaller, such that the generated load samples have a much smaller uncertainty compared to the network operational planning stage. The DSO can decide whether or not to activate a service by comparing the expected benefit of the service with the activation cost. The risk of the DSO deviating from this specified activation probability, by activating conditional services more or less often, is carried by the aggregators. Thus, aggregators have the incentive to specify their real reserve cost, as well as their real service activation cost in their bids."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-65c3762894-p08-c2r3__v141-a-M01-activation","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.4 Activation benefit evaluation for conditional services","anchor_text":"In the case of conditional services, the DSO has to pay an activationng fee to the aggregators. The ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the case of conditional services, the DSO has to pay an activation fee to the aggregators. The DSO has to make the decision whether it is beneficial to activate the service or not. ... The service activation signal can be sent up to one hour before the service delivery period. At this point, the uncertainty of load forecasts is smaller, as the delivery period is closer."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No x: the supplied settlement evidence defines no design selection or operational decision variable for the payment rule. Activation status is a condition that selects the applicable payment branch; its decision procedure is in the activation lead v141-a-M01-activation and is not defined or optimized as a variable at settlement.payment in this frozen graph.","empty_theta_reason":"No theta: the evidence quotes qualitative terms (reserve part, reserve price, activation part, activation fee, final activation cost) but gives no symbol, unit, domain or numeric value for any settlement parameter. The numeric activation-cost and activation-benefit formulas in the paper concern v141-a-M02 and are not attached to v141-c-R005."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-activation","v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e26","quote":"Activation costs are specified by the aggregators as part of their bids, hence the final activation cost is determined by the outcome of the market clearing."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e12","quote":"In the case of conditional services, the DSO has to pay an activation fee to the aggregators."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E02","quote":"Payments for conditional services are split into a reserve part and an activation part."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E02","quote":"If a conditional service is not activated, the DSO only pays the reserve price."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e26","quote":"In the case of conditional services, the DSO has to pay an activation fee to the aggregators."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E02","quote":"Payments for conditional services are split into a reserve part and an activation part. If a conditional service is not activated, the DSO only pays the reserve price."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"71bc47951d50081e5451e8564b00cbdf3d6b6a4635bde398fca25b0a1c7265a9","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule is a procedural settlement rule. The supplied same-mechanism evidence states the payment structure in prose: conditional-service payments are split into reserve and activation parts, only the reserve price is paid if the service is not activated, and an activation fee is paid to aggregators if the service is activated (v141-b-g01-E02, v141-b-g02-e26, v141-b-g03-e12). No equation, symbol definition, domain, unit or numerical parameter for the settlement calculation is supplied for this rule's nodes/edges. The quantitative activation-benefit and activation-probability formulas (3)-(6) using gamma_k^s, B_k^s and pi_act belong to the DSO methodology mechanism v141-a-M02 and are not evidence for v141-c-R005. Thus formalization is limited to preserving the procedural constraints.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","node_ids":["clearing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R005-E001"],"rationale":"C001 is the core settlement link: the local clearing outcome determines the final activation fee, matching the frozen edge from clearing.local to settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 describes the two-part payment structure at the settlement.payment node; no additional graph edge is asserted."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C003","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C003 is the not-activated branch of the same payment procedure at settlement.payment; no additional edge is asserted."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C004","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C004 is the activated branch of the same payment procedure at settlement.payment; no additional edge is asserted."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
